@startuml
title State Diagram - Parcel Status Lifecycle
caption SwiftDrop parcel-service (Role 3)

hide empty description
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  StartColor black
  EndColor black
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor black
  BackgroundColor white
}

state CREATED
state PICKED_UP
state IN_TRANSIT
state OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
state DELIVERED #C8E6C9
state FAILED #FFCDD2

CREATED : tracking number SD-XXXX-XXXX issued
CREATED : fee calculated by pricing-service
DELIVERED : final state
FAILED : final state
FAILED : failure_reason stored

[*] -down-> CREATED : customer booking (POST /api/v1/parcels)\nor merchant API order (POST /internal/parcels)
CREATED -down-> PICKED_UP : courier collects the parcel
PICKED_UP -down-> IN_TRANSIT : parcel moving between hubs
IN_TRANSIT -down-> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY : courier out on the delivery run
OUT_FOR_DELIVERY -down-> DELIVERED : recipient receives it\n[optional note / proof photo]
OUT_FOR_DELIVERY -right-> FAILED : delivery unsuccessful\n[failure reason required]
DELIVERED -down-> [*]
FAILED -down-> [*]

note left of PICKED_UP
  <b>On every transition (one database transaction)</b>
  - update parcels.status
  - insert a parcel_status_history row
    (who, role, when, note, proof reference)
  - insert an outbox event ParcelStatusChanged
    with routing key parcel.status.<new status>
  - the event later triggers email/SMS, the merchant
    webhook, report counters and the live tracking
    page (SSE)
end note

note right of PICKED_UP
  <b>Who can change status</b>
  After CREATED: the assigned courier,
  a dispatcher or an admin
  (via PATCH /internal/parcels/{id}/status,
  enforced by ParcelStateMachine)
end note

note right of IN_TRANSIT
  <b>Rejected requests (RFC 7807 ProblemDetail)</b>
  - missing or wrong X-Internal-Token
    -> 401 Unauthorized
  - transition not drawn here (skipping a state,
    going back, leaving DELIVERED or FAILED)
    -> 409 Conflict
  - FAILED without a reason, or a reason with
    any other status -> 400 Bad Request
  - courier not assigned to this parcel, or a role
    other than COURIER/DISPATCHER/ADMIN
    -> 403 Forbidden
  - unknown parcel id -> 404 Not Found
end note

note bottom of FAILED
  Reason is free text, e.g. recipient
  not available, wrong address,
  refused by recipient.
end note

@enduml
